WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:02.960
- [Narrator] Built in
the short economic boom

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.610
between two world wars,
the Zollverein Coal Mine

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:09.000
in Germany stands as a
reminder of an industry's past

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.643
and an architectural future.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:15.461
(bright music)

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.540
The Zollverein Mine
was decommissioned in 1986,

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.563
after being an active
mine for over 100 years.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.470
It was built with conscious thought

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.880
for the external appearance,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.310
and during redevelopments
and expansions in the 1920s,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:33.800
adopted a Bauhaus style of architecture,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.070
which features a modern
symmetrical and industrial feel

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.770
and combines form with function.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.240
Today it remains open to the
public as an industrial museum

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:47.050
and is protected as a
UNESCO World Heritage site.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.570
At Zollverein, much of
the former coal factory

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.230
has been left in tact,
allowing visitors to view

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.433
the pits, railway lines and
even the miners housing.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:58.850
It is truly a monument of industry

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.265
caught in a moment of history.

00:01:01.265 --> 00:01:03.932
(bright music)

